---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const [articles, passages, records, events, relationships, themes, images] = await Promise.all([
  getCollection("articles"), getCollection("passages"), getCollection("records"), getCollection("events"),
  getCollection("relationships"), getCollection("themes"), getCollection("images"),
]);
---
<SiteLayout title="About — A History of GIS in New Zealand" description="How the reader, connected content and editing workflow fit together.">
  <section class="page-wrap about-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this reader</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">A history that can keep growing</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">Stories lead. Linked records, themes, dates and images give readers other paths through the same changing collection.</p>
    <div class="about-counts" aria-label="Current sample size">
      <div><strong>{articles.length}</strong><span>stories</span></div><div><strong>{passages.length}</strong><span>passages</span></div>
      <div><strong>{records.length}</strong><span>records</span></div><div><strong>{events.length}</strong><span>events</span></div>
      <div><strong>{relationships.length}</strong><span>connections</span></div><div><strong>{themes.length}</strong><span>themes</span></div><div><strong>{images.length}</strong><span>images</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <h2>Reading and navigation</h2>
      <p>The opening reader uses the published AAM / AAMHatch and NorthSouth GIS NZ account. Theme choices filter passages and timeline moments. Timeline events jump to their related passages. The small contextual network stays beside the narrative; the larger Network view is optional.</p>
      <p>Your reading position and selected skin are stored in this browser. The timeline retains the date precision recorded with each event. A year-level date is labelled as a year.</p>
      <h2>Content updates</h2>
      <p>Editors add stories and passages as separate entries in the editing workspace. A passage links to records and themes. An event links to one or more passages, and a relationship links two records. New content appears after a reviewed site build. The model has no preset story or passage count.</p>
      <p>Images are local copies only where reuse terms allow it. Each image page records the source, credit and licence so the reading text stays uncluttered.</p>
      <h2>Suggest an update</h2>
      <p>There is no public submission form. Use the email link at the bottom of the page. It opens with the page address and prompts for the suggested change, source or memory, and related people or organisations.</p>
      <h2>Preview status</h2>
      <p>This clean-slate staging build is a small structural sample. The existing live publication remains unchanged. No deployment or production cutover is included in this work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
